  "bug_report_content": "{\"id\":787,\"status\":\"Fixed\",\"summary\":\"true/false are not always replaced for !0/!1\",\"labels\":[\"Type-Defect\",\"Priority-Medium\"],\"stars\":0,\"commentCount\":3,\"comments\":[{\"id\":0,\"commenterId\":-2177134355389785939,\"content\":\"\\u003cb\\u003eWhat steps will reproduce the problem?\\u003c/b\\u003e\\n\\r\\nfunction some_function() {\\r\\n  var fn1;\\r\\n  var fn2;\\r\\n\\r\\n  if (any_expression) {\\r\\n    fn2 \\u003d external_ref;\\r\\n    fn1 \\u003d function (content) {\\r\\n      return fn2();\\r\\n    }\\r\\n  }\\r\\n\\r\\n  return {\\r\\n    method1: function () {\\r\\n      if (fn1) fn1();\\r\\n      return true;\\r\\n    },\\r\\n    method2: function () {\\r\\n      return false;\\r\\n    }\\r\\n  }\\r\\n}\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003cb\\u003eWhat is the expected output? What do you see instead?\\u003c/b\\u003e\\n\\r\\nWe expect that true/false will be replaced for !0/!1, but it doesn\\u0027t happend.\\r\\n\\r\\nfunction some_function() {\\r\\n  var a, b;\\r\\n  any_expression \\u0026amp;\\u0026amp; (b \\u003d external_ref, a \\u003d function () {\\r\\n    return b()\\r\\n  });\\r\\n  return {\\r\\n    method1: function () {\\r\\n      a \\u0026amp;\\u0026amp; a();\\r\\n      return true\\r\\n    },\\r\\n    method2: function () {\\r\\n      return false\\r\\n    }\\r\\n  }\\r\\n};\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003cb\\u003eWhat version of the product are you using? On what operating system?\\u003c/b\\u003e\\n\\r\\nThis is output for latest official build.\\r\\nI also got the same output for 20120430, 20120305. But 20111117 is OK.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003cb\\u003ePlease provide any additional information below.\\u003c/b\\u003e\\n\\r\\nHere is just one of example. I found too many non-replaced true/false in compiler output. Replacement non-replaced true/false to !1/!0 in conpiler output saves 1-2 kb for 850 kb js file.\",\"timestamp\":1343813264,\"attachments\":[]},{\"id\":1,\"commenterId\":-5060162230523776870,\"content\":\"The peephole optimizations are being short circuited, I\\u0027m pretty sure I caused this problem so I\\u0027ll look into it.\",\"timestamp\":1343847526,\"attachments\":[]},{\"id\":2,\"commenterId\":-7699928860083865744,\"content\":\"This issue was closed by revision r2119.\",\"timestamp\":1344005344,\"attachments\":[]}]}",
